; RESOLVED: iota is a stdlib .esk function (lib/core/list/generate.esk),
; not a real native dispatch target; fid 141 in the BUILTINS[] tables has no
; dispatcher case on either backend and was always a vestigial registration,
; shadowed by the real definition once loaded. The actual defect was that
; the VM's always-available embedded prelude (lib/backend/vm_prelude_source.h,
; used whenever a program says `(require stdlib)` rather than the explicit
; `(require core.list.generate)`) never defined `iota` at all, so the
; vestigial fid-141 closure was the only thing left bound to the name and
; printed "WARNING: unhandled native call ID 141" plus (). `iota` is now
; defined directly in the VM prelude with full SRFI-1 (count [start [step]])
; semantics, matching lib/core/list/generate.esk exactly on both routes.
; native -r : (0 1 2 3)
; vm        : (0 1 2 3)
(display (iota 4))
